    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1402">

                <pb facs="1748" n="1548" sameAs="frus:frus1945Berlinv02/pg1548"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.00119 Potsdam/8–645: Telegram</note>
                <head>No. 1402<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in France</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                    >Caffery</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Acting
                            Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left"><hi rendition="#small-caps">top secret</hi></seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Paris</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1945-08-06T16:00:00+02:00">August 6, 1945—4 p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>4722. Bidault tells me confidentially that
                    replies to the various notes I handed to him having to do with the Potsdam
                        Conference<anchor n="1" xml:id="d1402-f1"/> will be handed to me within the
                    next day or two. He remarked that his government is very much upset over the
                    statements regarding reparations which they read in the Potsdam
                        communiqué.<anchor n="2" xml:id="d1402-f2"/> He said that they are also much
                    concerned about the article referring to the <pb facs="1749" n="1549"
                        xml:id="pg1549"/> possibility of setting up a central government for
                        Germany<anchor n="3" xml:id="d1402-f3"/> for they take it to mean that it is
                    the intention of the Soviet Government to Sovietize all Germany as rapidly as
                    they can do so.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                            >Caffery</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
